WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.320
It's no secret there's
lots of money to be made

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.850
owning a sports team.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.450
Media deals and fan enthusiasm soaring,

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.880
it's been really hard not to make money.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.330
Now, with more cash than ever

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.460
vying for a place in pro sports

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.010
and a reckoning around equality
and opportunity underway,

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.740
the biggest payday may be on
the women's side of the game.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.853
Alex Morgan!

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.660
I look at the women's sports market

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.830
similar to venture.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.010
There's a lot more upside.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.730
Woo! How'd that go in?

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.930
Female athletes and fans

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.680
have been trailblazing this
change for generations.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.520
Historically, and more recently,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.470
it's been a painful process

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.550
as women fight institutions and systems

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.830
seemingly designed to diminish and,

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.620
even at times, abuse them.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.410
It's not just a basic
issue of right and wrong,

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:53.300
but also a question about power and money,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.560
and the conversation around
how to invest in women's sports

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.600
and who is writing the checks

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.290
has taken on a different
urgency and dimension,

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.160
perhaps leading to a new
and very lucrative era

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.770
of opportunity.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.420
Imagine if you had a
chance to go back in time

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.100
and by the Boston Celtics in 1957.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.180
If you make the investment now,

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.100
given how low franchise prices are,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.550
I would expect, in 20, 25 years,

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.160
your investment's gonna
be worth, you know,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.353
many, many times what
you just paid for it.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.610
So, we're here in Los Angeles,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.770
on a freeway, naturally.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.520
This is one of the great sports towns,

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.650
some of the most notable
franchises across all sports.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.540
You think about the Lakers,
you think about the Dodgers.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.530
Everyone seems, though,

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.540
to be talking about the
newest team on the scene,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.740
and that's Angel City.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.190
The Women's soccer team

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.780
is coming to Los Angeles, all
thanks to Natalle Portman.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.140
Angel City FC is the product

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.020
of actress and activist Natalle Portman

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.350
and Kara Nortman,

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.870
a partner at an early
stage investment firm.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.130
They made headlines last year

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.010
when they announced plans

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.240
to bring in national women's
soccer league team to LA.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.030
Their star-studded list of investors

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.910
includes Jennifer
Garner, Jessica Chastain,

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.937
America Ferrera,

00:02:06.937 --> 00:02:09.970
Uzo Aduba, and Eva Longoria.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.600
The leading founding
investor is Alexis Ohanian.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.930
He's the co-founder of Reddit,

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.990
and, of course, the
husband to Serena Williams.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.560
Their toddler daughter,
Alexis Olympia Ohanian,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.320
is also an investor.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.170
They brought in a third
co-founder to run the team,

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.390
a veteran of building businesses.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.960
Her name is Julie Uhrman,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:31.060
and right now, she's still
building out their office space.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.700
So, this is a real startup.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.100
I mean,

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.410
we're still waiting for Fiverr.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.560
Hi! How are you? Good to see you!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.760
Yeah, this is the future
home of Angel City.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.480
So, we've got two big
conference rooms here.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.910
Then we'll call this the bullpen,

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.700
for lack of a better term right now.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.600
I have to start using
more soccer references

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.410
than other sports.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.580
What's really neat with this blank wall

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.030
is we'll have a projector

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.540
so we can project games on the wall,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.260
but we're gonna have pull-down,

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.920
so we'll have a pull down green screen,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.250
pull down widescreen, and
a pull-down step and repeat

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.160
so that we can do content
shoots here, merch shoots here.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.240
When we have player signings,

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:10.270
we can just create the atmosphere here.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.420
Uhrman's a native Angelino

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.210
who came up through media and technology

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.380
and has a knack for
getting into businesses

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.140
at points of inflection.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.270
I was an entrepreneur in college.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.350
My stepfather was an entrepreneur.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.310
You know, he taught us
two things growing up.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.300
The first was work for yourself

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.850
and be in control of your own destiny,

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.080
and, if you can't work for yourself,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.030
be on the revenue side of the business.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.560
While valuations have continued to rise

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.472
in a lot of sports,

00:03:38.472 --> 00:03:41.090
this is a tough business in many ways,

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.320
and it's an especially tough business

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.050
when it comes to
professional women's sports.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.480
This is not for the faint
of heart, in many ways.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.090
Over 90% of all sports teams
globally don't make money,

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.607
and so, we looked at all
this information and said,

00:03:55.607 --> 00:03:57.540
"We're female founders, that's different.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.410
We're gonna raise money
like it's a startup,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.330
which is different.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.810
We're gonna drive to profitability

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.260
'cause if we can show we can make money

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.560
being different in those other ways,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.100
that's gonna be pretty significant."

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.370
Julie Uhrman sent me a LinkedIn message,

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.400
and was just like, "Hey,
I hear you're the woman

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.960
to talk to in sponsorship,

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.150
and I'd love to talk
to you about an idea."

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.040
This is Jess Smith.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.320
She's the head of revenue for Angel City,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.640
and her idea was to blend
Angel City's goal of profit

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.210
with social impact.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.320
I put together a business
proposal for her,

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.690
and said, "Hey, this is how I think

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.620
you should go to market,"

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.870
and it was really that, if
you're gonna walk in a room

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.710
and tell people that
you're standing for change,

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.210
how do you hold yourself accountable,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.010
and also, the partner accountable,

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.650
and really, the way to do
that is through dollars.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.170
When we started talking to brands,

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.440
we also launched the Angel
City sponsorship model,

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.510
where we give 10% of
our sponsorship dollars

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.130
back into the community through
our social impact platform.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.070
So, when Angel City
sells their front of kit

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.760
sponsorship to Door Dash,

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.170
10% of that sale goes

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.300
to combating food
insecurity in Los Angeles.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.800
This purpose driven advertising

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.570
has helped to attract the
likes of Birdies, Heineken,

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.810
Tecate, and Gatorade.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:03.700
We said from the beginning

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.930
we wanted to build an organization

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.630
where mission to capital could coexist,

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.610
so what does that mean?

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.820
It means that we want to
set higher expectations.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.050
What does that mean, right?

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.560
It means that we lead
with passion and purpose

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.760
to drive to profitability,

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.670
and that is the key sentence

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.193
that we make decisions
based on every single day.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.070
Recently though,

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.380
Angel City's impact in the world of sports

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:30.600
would take on an added importance.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.990
The national women's soccer league

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.960
faces a reckoning overcharges
that it ignored abuse

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:35.980
of its players.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.090
Former NWSL players have
accused former coach Paul Riley

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.600
of sexual coercion.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.530
A stark reminder of just how backwards

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.540
and broken parts of the system are

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.020
came in late September,

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.170
when The Athletic
published an investigation

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:52.090
detailing allegations
of sexual misconduct,

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:55.050
including harassment and coerced sex.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.480
It also detailed how earlier accusations

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:01.010
weren't fully investigated
or disciplined by the league.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:04.443
Our institution failed
us, the system, right?

00:06:04.443 --> 00:06:07.590
It's the people in power,
not just the coach,

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.810
but the leadership team.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.620
Paul Riley couldn't be
reached for comment,

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.900
and has denied the allegations.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.670
The league suspended play for the weekend

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.830
after The Athletic report published,

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.120
and forced the resignation of
the commissioner, Lisa Baird.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.620
She said in a statement

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.230
that she takes full responsibility

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.330
for her role in the allegations

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.870
and is sorry for the
pain many are feeling.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.640
Social media was filled
with indignation and anger,

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.500
including from Megan
Rapinoe, who tweeted, quote,

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.050
burn it all down.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:38.210
Let all their heads roll.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.410
I hope we're in a real moment of reckoning

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.860
where we can turn this into real change

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.100
and hopefully save the league,

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.200
'cause, as it stands right now,

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.590
that's not really league any
of us wanna be a part of.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.340
Angel City may be part of that change.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.030
Sinead Farrelly whose
allegations of long-term abuse

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.890
were detailed in The Athletic

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:59.593
cited Angel City as part of
her inspiration to go public.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.470
I think I started reading the article

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:07.800
at 5:15 in the morning, Pacific time,

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:09.010
and I don't think I've ever done this,

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.350
but I was in and out of tears all day.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:12.183
This is Angela Hucles,

00:07:12.183 --> 00:07:14.790
a two time gold medalist for US soccer

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.390
and founding investor for Angel City.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:20.390
This is something that affects all of us.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.420
It doesn't just affect
the soccer community.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.950
This is something that
we are struggling with

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.130
in our society and the world,

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.710
and this is something
that we need to get right.

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:30.870
US Soccer Federation

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.870
which governs the NWSL

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.890
retained former deputy
attorney general Sally Yates

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.610
to lead an investigation into the league

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:41.343
as it hopes to rebuild
its trust with players.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.870
For me, and, I think, our organization

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.810
and that we're continuing
to do on the daily

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.840
its to make sure that
we are moving forward

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.850
and providing a better environment

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:55.520
and a place that is stronger
than it's ever been before,

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.060
to make sure that these women can play,

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.260
and be celebrated, and feel safe,

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.963
and that's not an
unacceptable thing to ask for.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.680
The harsh reality for the NWSL

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.740
is not only does it need
to regain the support

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.500
and trust of its players,

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.220
but it will also need time to develop

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.410
its fan and sponsor base.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.160
And if it's looking for a role model,

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.010
look no further than the WNBA.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:21.660
Reiner finds Taurasi at three!

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:25.613
It's gone! She got it!
The GOAT delivers again!

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.250
At 25 years old,

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.430
the league is one of the
oldest, most well-known,

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.670
and most successful women's
sports leagues in the world.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:37.180
And its stars are getting
more attention than ever.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.550
Whether it's from activism
efforts around the league,

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.300
or more blue chip advertisers

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.960
featuring them in commercials.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:44.310
I sold a car to Sue Bird.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.743
11 all-star appearances. Can you imagine?

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.740
I mean, I'm working on it.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.340
But if you measure the
WNBA against the NBA,

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.180
it's still a massive gap.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.150
Attendance for the NBA averages
more than 17,000 a game,

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:04.020
while the WNBA averages
between six and 7,000,

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.520
and estimates of the
combined revenue for the NBA,

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.740
it's about $7.9 billion

00:09:09.718 --> 00:09:12.890
versus the WNBA at 60 million.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:15.580
I think the big issue people
have with women's sports

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.410
is that, relative to men's
sports, it's a lot smaller.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.620
This is David Berry.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.820
He's a professor who's written extensively

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.620
about the economics of sports,

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.530
especially women's sports,

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:27.220
and he argues that the biggest factor

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:30.550
between men and women's leagues is time.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.980
WNBA is smaller because
it's only 25 years old,

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.560
and, if you look at the NBA
when it was 25 years old,

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:39.040
it looks a lot like the WNBA today.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.060
The NBA back in the late 1960s

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.340
was getting about six, 7,000 fans a game.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:46.570
Nobody really paid much
attention to the league,

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.280
and, in 25, 30 years,

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.453
WNBA's gonna look a lot like the NBA.

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.930
As David explains, this
decades long growth

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:58.760
has been true in almost all pro sports.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.690
It usually takes generations

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:03.420
to develop emotional attachment to teams.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.040
Take the Pittsburgh Steelers

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.150
who were purchased by Art Rooney in 1933

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:12.640
for a whopping $53,000 in today's dollars.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.090
Art Rooney is investing in a sports league

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.240
where 85 to 90% of the previous franchises

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.850
completely went out of business,

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:22.150
but he does it anyways.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:24.900
He loves football, so he puts
his money into this thing.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.740
For 40 years, Rooney kept putting money

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.880
into a Steelers franchise
that won nothing.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.190
They went to one playoff game at 40 years,

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.430
and, in that playoff game,
they scored no points.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.330
He never saw a playoff point for 40 years,

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.360
and he kept putting money into it.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.740
Eventually, a fan base develops,

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.020
people become emotionally attached to it,

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.580
and the Steelers that are
inherited by his grandson

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.710
are worth a billion dollars.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.590
And nearly two decades later,

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.953
Art Rooney II's franchise
is worth $3.4 billion.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.900
Ownership is an area Angel
City thinks it can improve on.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.490
Instead of having its future rest

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.310
on the shoulders of one owner,

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.470
it instead has a diversified ownership

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.340
across a large group,

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.860
including an all-star
list of former players.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.550
We're but budding seeds,

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.830
except, this time, we're owners!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.720
It started in an email, really.

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.400
Julie Foudy, Mia Hamm sent to the rest

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:21.970
of some of the players

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:24.670
about this opportunity
to invest in Angel City

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:27.610
and bringing women's professional
soccer to Los Angeles.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:30.450
I think it was probably
the quickest response

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:34.380
that I've seen from
about, you know, 10 women.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:37.100
And that ownership group would only grow.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.760
We have over 60 owners.
They're all incredible.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.850
They all bring something
different to the platform.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.030
I was telling someone the other day

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:45.220
that I literally don't
think there is an owner

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.250
that hasn't done something for Angel City.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.270
The story I've told in
some rooms about that

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.580
is being in a sponsorship
pitch, talking to a beer brand,

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:53.740
and a gentleman's in the room.

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:56.280
He says, "Hey, I'm from the
lifestyle side of the brand,

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.160
and, candidly, I don't follow sports,

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.120
but I have to tell you,

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.590
I know everything about Angel City

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.500
because I follow Sophia Bush,"

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.110
and what's really incredible
about our ownership group,

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:07.210
when you think about
the power of Angel City,

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.560
is that each one of them
has their own audience,

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.180
and each one of them are
sharing things about us

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.630
and aligning with us on things

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.950
that they're passionate about.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.320
And the expectation,

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.860
when they invested in Angel City,

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.017
was you have to care about the purpose

00:12:20.017 --> 00:12:23.640
and you have to be available to help us,

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.740
you know, grow the business,

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.940
and have a positive
impact on our community,

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.300
and everybody signed up for that.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.970
But beyond passion for owners,

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.960
for more money to continue
to flow into women's sports,

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:36.290
it's going to need more evidence
that it can be successful,

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.643
and, for investors, that means data.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.240
Everyone's heard of the money ball effect.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.200
You know, we're increasingly using data

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.540
to help our players get the
most out of their careers,

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.390
out of their performance,

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.220
and, on the business side of sports,

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.807
unfortunately, there's been a lot of just,

00:12:55.807 --> 00:12:58.070
"Hey, that's how we've
always done business."

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.950
Angela Ruggiero has played more games

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:03.120
in a USA hockey Jersey
than any man or woman,

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.750
winning gold, silver, and bronze medals.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.870
After her career on the ice,

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.800
she got an MBA at Harvard

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.010
and set up Sports Innovation Lab.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:13.560
It's a Boston based company
that uses data science

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.440
to help teams and leagues

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.620
understand their fans

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.000
and figure out how to better engage them,

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.610
and, to be clear, to
help them find new ways

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.400
to make revenue off them.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.530
We watch sports differently.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.180
I watch sports differently.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.870
Half the time, I have my
second screen in my hand,

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.520
I'm flipping through scores,

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:33.130
checking out highlights, got my red zone,

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:34.390
maybe I'm on Twitch over here.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.440
Where we're doing things very differently.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.180
We're all shifting in how we consume,

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.340
contribute to sports, create content,

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:44.870
interact with athletes,
model shifting overnight.

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:48.240
In the early days of the sports industry,

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.150
you had a very localized fan,

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.630
so ticket sales were really

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:55.030
the biggest proponent of revenue.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:58.030
Then, as you start to move
into the 1940s and 50s,

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.000
you have the advent of broadcast media

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.930
that allows for fans to start

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.450
following more than just their local team,

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.940
and that also starts to translate

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:09.920
into them becoming more
consumers of sports,

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.480
so they start buying.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.530
You start seeing merchandising
and sponsorship opportunities

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.840
start to really take off.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.960
And now what we've really moved into

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.500
in this digital age,

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.470
with the advent of the internet,

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:24.710
of smartphones, of social media,

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:27.900
we're moving into what we
call the age of the fluid fan.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:28.733
And they believe that,

00:14:28.733 --> 00:14:30.390
just as the advent of television

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.260
helped fuel new areas of revenue

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.520
in the age of the global fan,

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.870
new technology and social platforms

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:40.050
will do the same in the
age of the fluid fan.

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:43.310
We see an evolving media landscape

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:47.790
where all fans want
more than just the game.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.840
Now they want more online,

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.740
they wanna understand the athletes,

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.770
they want that Netflix docuseries,

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:59.110
but fans of women's sports,
per the fan project data,

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:02.190
suggests that they want it more.

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:04.490
In a report published earlier this year,

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:06.480
SIL outlines how fans of women's sports

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.780
are ahead of the curve

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:11.010
when it comes to how
technology is changing fandom.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.980
You can't be a lazy women's sports fan.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:15.820
You can't just turn on the game,

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:19.647
you can't just find your
content wherever you want.

00:15:19.647 --> 00:15:23.350
We've almost forced
the hand of this market

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:24.760
to be digitally savvy.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.590
We forced the hand of this market

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.610
to behave in ways, maybe
they were uncomfortable,

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.980
but they got over that hurdle

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.570
and they were the first to do it.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:37.620
What that gives us is
this incredible group

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.880
of what we call early adopters,

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.990
and this has been used in
other industries before.

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:44.700
Sometimes, they're called hyper users.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.150
When I was at Spotify, we
called them trendsetters,

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.410
but essentially, what
you need to understand

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:50.830
about early adopters

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:53.310
is that, typically,
they will only represent

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:56.120
one to 10% of a given fan base.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.860
They can represent as much as 50 to 80%

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.010
of the revenue potential
that you can drive.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.730
And while there's
potentially a lot of money

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.440
to be made in understanding

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.620
the behavior of women's sports fans,

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.220
the report also made clear

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:11.700
there's a big opportunity in
women's sports themselves.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.040
In our analysis,

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.770
we looked at a number of sources

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:19.770
that predicted the global
sports business market

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.200
would be around 800 billion by 2030.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.290
We believe, if we invest
in women's sports now,

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.760
the opportunity for women's sports

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:31.910
could be a third of that
$800 billion market.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.020
In its report, SIL proposes

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:38.310
what it calls a community-based
monetization model.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.630
It outlines how women's sports

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.870
can capitalize on this
shifting fan behavior

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.420
by producing more story-driven content,

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:47.290
distributing it on new,
emerging platforms,

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:50.570
and measuring quality of
engagement over quantity.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.090
You have to approach this market

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.900
with a focus on it's a different fan.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:57.820
Don't just take the same
model, do it differently,

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.280
build out your revenue in new ways,

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.340
and that actually is gonna
unlock, in our opinion,

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:05.930
not just a better ROI, better return,

00:17:05.930 --> 00:17:07.550
but also it's where the puck is headed,

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:09.200
if I can use a hockey analogy.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:13.360
You've actually created a
market of your future consumer.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.290
That's your current fan of women's sports.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.390
They're already there.

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.640
Angel City won't play any games here

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:26.010
at Bank of California Stadium
until the spring of 2022,

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.750
and while they have good financial backing

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:29.940
and have made early sponsorship deals,

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:32.620
they're still going to
need to attract fans,

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:35.800
and the best path to that
is through their players.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.640
We think fandom has really changed,

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.660
and it's changed, mostly,
because of social media,

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.150
where I'm a fan of the player first,

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.530
their team second, and
then the league third,

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.280
and so, when you think about the asset

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:47.950
that is most valuable to you

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.750
being your 22, 24 person roster,

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.030
the way that I can create a
connection with that player

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:55.120
that can then translate to the club

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.880
and then allow us the ability to monetize

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:00.240
is to tell the story
of who that player is.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.480
Good morning, Angel City fans.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.760
I am so excited to be coming home.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:06.583
I hope to see you soon!

00:18:06.583 --> 00:18:07.910
And, for Angel City,

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.670
they needed a star,

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.210
and it's hard to find a better option

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.960
than LA's own Christen Press.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.713
And Press, there it is!

00:18:16.713 --> 00:18:18.443
The moment they've been waiting for!

00:18:18.443 --> 00:18:19.990
A native of Southern California,

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.400
she's Angel City's first

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.600
and currently only player on the roster,

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.230
and before Angel City plays
any games on the pitch,

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.150
they'll rely on Press
to help build awareness.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.480
That's especially important for a new team

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:35.480
in a nine-year-old circuit
that's the third try

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.400
at a US pro women's soccer league.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.070
I may not know there's an NWSL.

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:42.390
I may not know there's a
national women's soccer league,

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.020
but I know there's an Alex Morgan,

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.710
I know Megan Rapinoe,
I know Christen press,

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.130
and when I start to follow them,

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.070
then I find out,

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:52.370
Oh, wait, they play for the Orlando Pride,

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:55.130
or they are soon to play for Angel City.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.370
Angel City will need a roster

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:58.460
full of name recognition like Press

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:00.850
to drive interest to their team.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:04.460
That has been the theory on
the NWSL from its inception,

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:07.180
to connect the popularity
and historic success

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.130
of the US Women's National Team

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:11.460
to a more traditional league.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.380
But at a time when player
trust in that league

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.730
is being challenged,

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.940
Angel City is attempting
to help provide support

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.910
for all women's soccer players,

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.483
both future and past.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.210
They've been producing a profile series

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.650
around young talent in the LA area,

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.160
and recently announced a
plan to create a players fund

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.320
so the retiring professional players

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:33.190
can receive money for education
in their post-career life.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.150
There is a huge gap right now

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.800
from the time that you retire

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.490
to the time that you are entering

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:42.630
into your next career path,

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.290
so that's one of the things

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.150
and ways that we like to
think about player care,

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:50.300
is, you know, looking at
that player holistically,

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.530
and it's not just about the time

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:54.170
that they're playing in the
league, but it's, you know,

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.300
what are they doing afterwards,

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:59.320
and how can we help to foster and connect

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.743
that community as well?

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.450
It's an acknowledgement

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:07.120
that while the early returns
look good for Angel City,

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.390
this is a long-term
investment in the sport,

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.720
and that they're committed, not only,

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.630
to fielding a successful team,

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:15.880
but building a successful
sports ecosystem.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.923
One that goes beyond their team
or even the current league.

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:22.540
Our aspiration is to be a global brand,

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:23.733
and it's been our aspiration from day one,

00:20:23.733 --> 00:20:26.800
and the reason is, because,
if you're a global brand,

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.450
you could have the most impact.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:30.380
Full-stop.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:33.180
It's a platform that stands
for equality and impact,

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:36.200
and if we can develop a
relationship with our community

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.270
that goes way beyond wins and losses,

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:40.370
we have the ability to impact their lives.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.800
The future of the NWSL

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.470
may remain in question for some time,

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.510
but it's clear from the
outpouring of support from fans

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:52.290
that they intend to support the players

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:54.960
wherever they ultimately play,

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.430
and it's never been more
clear that who funds,

00:20:57.430 --> 00:21:00.400
and, ultimately, who
profits from women's sports

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.420
have the opportunity
to make big changes in,

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.030
not just sports, but society.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.210
Yes, women's sports is
the right thing to do.

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:09.900
Yes, we should be investing in women.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.890
We should be creating role
models for all of society.

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:14.530
Yes, check, check, check,

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:16.010
but there's more than that.

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:18.430
Women's sports is actually a big business.

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:19.940
It's unlocking revenue,

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:22.600
it's unlocking potential understanding

00:21:22.600 --> 00:21:25.230
of where fandom in general is going,

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:27.550
but you have an opportunity to get in now

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:28.980
with women's sports.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:30.730
And, from an investment perspective,

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.070
it's one of the biggest differences

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:34.200
between men's and women's sports.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:36.270
For the most popular sports in the world,

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.940
to buy into a team in the men's space

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.490
is maybe one of the
hardest deals to close,

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:41.940
but, for those same sports,

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.493
the women's game is open for business.

